                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Dreport uses /tmp as a temporary location for files. Consequently, every dreport log contains an incomplete list of dump-specific files. This approach can be applied to other use cases as well. Could you provide any specific reasons for implementing these changes?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "The problem we have hit in the past is contents missing (mainly journal) in the dump tar because there was no space left. lets add such useful cases."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rohit PAI ",
                        "email": "rohitpai77@gmail.com",
                        "username": "rohitpai"
                    },
                    "message": "lets avoid logs in commit message which are not really useful. like journal logs here."
